Error [E0357]: Pattern binding `FILE_EXT` must be snake_case
  --> pattern_hole_reuse_constant.jet:4:27
    |
  4 |     print(value == "main.{FILE_EXT}")
    |                           ^^^^^^^^
 Why: Jet enforces PascalCase for type-like names, snake_case for value-like names, and ALL_CAPS (SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE) for module-global constants (D-SHAPE-CASE1)
 Fix: Rename it to `file_ext`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0357

Error [E0118]: Pattern hole `{FILE_EXT}` would make a new `FILE_EXT`, but `FILE_EXT` already holds a value
  --> pattern_hole_reuse_constant.jet:4:27
    |
  4 |     print(value == "main.{FILE_EXT}")
    |                           ^^^^^^^^
 Why: A pattern hole introduces a new name; it does not compare with an existing value or refine it
 Fix: Wrap the pattern text in parentheses to compare with the existing value, or pick a new hole name to capture
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0118
